          "role": "primary",
          "dependency_reason": ""
        },
        {
          "unit_id": "u-9dc9e88ae722c8cbe085",
          "start_line": 185,
          "end_line": 205,
          "role": "primary",
          "dependency_reason": ""
        }
      ]
    ,
      "absence_claim": false,
      "audited_unit_ids": []
    },
    {
      "topic": "configuration",
      "statement": "The parameter generator selects windowLog and hashLog from ranges ending at 15, then passes those parameters to ZSTD_adjustCParams. FUZZ_setRandomParameters sets the resulting values on the compression context.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "unit_id": "u-194debf8ea4cd55b47ba",
          "start_line": 44,
          "end_line": 56,
          "role": "primary",
          "dependency_reason": ""
        },
        {
          "unit_id": "u-194debf8ea4cd55b47ba",
          "start_line": 101,
          "end_line": 110,
          "role": "dependency",
          "dependency_reason": "This caller applies the generated window and hash logs to the context."
        }
      ],
      "absence_claim": false,
      "audited_unit_ids": []
    },
    {
      "topic": "contract",
      "statement": "In both supplied versions, ZSTD_adjustCParams_internal can lower windowLog for a small source, lower hashLog according to the dictionary and window size, and impose further hash limits for tagged dictionary indices or row matching. For a zero size dictionary, ZSTD_dictAndWindowLog returns windowLog. The after version additionally cascades excluded compression strategies; that cascade does not itself set either log.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "unit_id": "u-facf31de921eddbcf157",
          "start_line": 1497,
          "end_line": 1553,
          "role": "primary",
          "dependency_reason": ""
        },
        {
          "unit_id": "u-31b9fce4fcddd0beca8e",
          "start_line": 1470,
          "end_line": 1595,
          "role": "primary",
          "dependency_reason": ""
        },
        {
          "unit_id": "u-c17e4af6c259fa3a3be5",
          "start_line": 1426,
          "end_line": 1432,
          "role": "dependency",
          "dependency_reason": "The adjustment calls this helper to obtain the dictionary and window log used in its hash limit."
        }
      ],
      "absence_claim": false,
      "audited_unit_ids": []
    },
    {
      "topic": "trigger",
      "statement": "The range producer can select any result generated from the supplied min and max and consumes bytes from the producer's end. This explains how finite fuzz bytes can choose values within the harness's ranges, but the supplied lines do not establish that a log above 15 is valid in the effective build.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "unit_id": "u-7eca6778229ce19a7b95",
          "start_line": 29,
          "end_line": 49,
          "role": "primary",
          "dependency_reason": ""
        },
        {
          "unit_id": "u-194debf8ea4cd55b47ba",
          "start_line": 44,
          "end_line": 56,
          "role": "dependency",
          "dependency_reason": "These are the actual ranges supplied to the producer for windowLog and hashLog."
        }
      ],
      "absence_claim": false,
      "audited_unit_ids": []
    },
    {
      "topic": "alternative",
      "statement": "The helper separately permits ZSTD_c_ldmHashLog up to 16 and varies ZSTD_c_forceMaxWindow. Those are possible related routes to assess, but the cited calls set parameters distinct from ZSTD_c_windowLog and ZSTD_c_hashLog.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "unit_id": "u-194debf8ea4cd55b47ba",
          "start_line": 103,
          "end_line": 105,
          "role": "primary",
          "dependency_reason": ""
        },
        {
          "unit_id": "u-194debf8ea4cd55b47ba",
          "start_line": 115,
          "end_line": 117,
          "role": "primary",
          "dependency_reason": ""
        },
        {
          "unit_id": "u-194debf8ea4cd55b47ba",
          "start_line": 138,
          "end_line": 140,
          "role": "primary",
          "dependency_reason": ""
        }
      ],
      "absence_claim": false,
      "audited_unit_ids": []
    },
    {
      "topic": "alternative",
      "statement": "Within the fully supplied old entry and parameter helper, there is no direct call that sets ZSTD_c_windowLog or ZSTD_c_hashLog above the generated values. A completed frame may reset the session and regenerate parameters, using the same helper.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "unit_id": "u-9dc9e88ae722c8cbe085",
